{"title":"Career roadmap · Stylist","role":"Stylist","summary":"A Stylist develops and coordinates the overall visual appearance of a person, fashion collection, campaign, editorial, advertisement, film/TV production, event, or brand. The role combines fashion knowledge, trend research, garment coordination, colour, silhouettes, accessories, visual storytelling, client communication, sourcing, budgeting, and creative direction.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)"},"about":[{"label":"Design pathway","text":"Fashion Design"},{"label":"Primary foundation","text":"Fashion design + styling + visual communication + trend forecasting"},{"label":"Important career reality","text":"Stylist is a portfolio- and network-driven profession. Graduates commonly begin as Styling Assistants, Fashion Assistants, Wardrobe Assistants, Junior Stylists or Fashion Coordinators before becoming independent or lead stylists."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build fashion, styling, garment, trend and portfolio fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Work as a styling/fashion assistant or junior stylist and develop a recognisable visual style"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Lead editorial, commercial, celebrity, e-commerce or campaign styling projects"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine styling with creative direction, technology, sustainability, AI and fashion-business expertise"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Fashion Design","Styling Internship","Styling/Fashion Assistant","Junior Stylist","Stylist","Senior/Fashion Stylist","Creative/Fashion Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"A Fashion Design degree provides a strong foundation, but the student should deliberately build styling, photography, editorial, merchandising and production skills in addition to garment design."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Fashion fundamentals, colour, silhouettes and visual observation"},{"text":"Fashion-design studio exercises"},{"text":"Styling mood boards + visual research book"},{"text":"Fashion foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Garment construction, textiles and fashion history"},{"text":"Textile/garment projects"},{"text":"Fabric and silhouette portfolio"},{"text":"Product knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Styling principles, trend research and wardrobe coordination"},{"text":"Editorial and commercial styling projects"},{"text":"3–5 complete styling stories"},{"text":"Styling capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Photography, makeup/hair coordination and accessories"},{"text":"Fashion shoots"},{"text":"Editorial photoshoot portfolio"},{"text":"Visual storytelling"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Brand styling, e-commerce and digital content"},{"text":"Commercial fashion projects"},{"text":"E-commerce/editorial case study"},{"text":"Commercial readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Internship, sourcing and production coordination"},{"text":"Styling studio/brand experience"},{"text":"Internship + styling credits"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced styling and creative direction"},{"text":"Major fashion project"},{"text":"5–8 polished styling cases"},{"text":"Professional portfolio"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Industry transition, networking and freelance practice"},{"text":"Client projects + portfolio reviews"},{"text":"Portfolio + showreel + industry contacts"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful foundations can be supplemented through Adobe Creative Cloud for visual editing and Figma for digital mood boards, presentations and visual systems.","url":"https://www.adobe.com/creativecloud.html"},{"type":"h","text":"Core fashion and styling stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Fashion fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fashion history"},{"text":"Fashion terminology"},{"text":"Garment construction"},{"text":"Silhouettes"},{"text":"Proportion"},{"text":"Fit"},{"text":"Fabric characteristics"},{"text":"Textile behaviour"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Prints"},{"text":"Patterns"},{"text":"Fashion seasons"},{"text":"Contemporary fashion trends"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A stylist must understand how garments behave on a body, not simply whether an outfit looks attractive on a mood board."}]},{"heading":"Styling fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Personal styling"},{"text":"Editorial styling"},{"text":"Commercial styling"},{"text":"Celebrity styling"},{"text":"E-commerce styling"},{"text":"Runway styling"},{"text":"Campaign styling"},{"text":"Wardrobe planning"},{"text":"Outfit coordination"},{"text":"Layering"},{"text":"Colour coordination"},{"text":"Silhouette balancing"},{"text":"Accessory coordination"},{"text":"Footwear selection"},{"text":"Jewellery selection"},{"text":"Bags and other fashion accessories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Person","Garment","Body Proportion","Colour","Context","Occasion","Brand","Camera"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Body proportions and fit","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Body proportions"},{"text":"Garment fit"},{"text":"Silhouette"},{"text":"Length"},{"text":"Volume"},{"text":"Layering"},{"text":"Necklines"},{"text":"Sleeves"},{"text":"Waist placement"},{"text":"Trouser/skirt proportions"},{"text":"Visual balance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid treating body types as rigid rules. Professional styling should focus on client preferences, comfort, context, desired visual effect and garment fit."}]},{"heading":"Colour and visual coordination","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Colour wheel"},{"text":"Complementary colours"},{"text":"Analogous colours"},{"text":"Monochromatic styling"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Warm/cool combinations"},{"text":"Neutrals"},{"text":"Seasonal palettes"},{"text":"Brand colour systems"},{"text":"Skin-tone considerations without rigid assumptions"},{"text":"Colour under studio lighting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create styling boards showing multiple colour directions for the same garment or client."}]},{"heading":"Textiles and materials","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Know the practical behaviour of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cotton"},{"text":"Linen"},{"text":"Silk"},{"text":"Wool"},{"text":"Denim"},{"text":"Leather"},{"text":"Rayon/viscose"},{"text":"Polyester"},{"text":"Nylon"},{"text":"Blends"},{"text":"Knits"},{"text":"Technical fabrics"},{"text":"Sustainable/recycled materials"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drape"},{"text":"Stretch"},{"text":"Weight"},{"text":"Texture"},{"text":"Sheen"},{"text":"Opacity"},{"text":"Wrinkling"},{"text":"Breathability"},{"text":"Care requirements"}]}]},{"heading":"Fashion trend forecasting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to research:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Runway trends"},{"text":"Street style"},{"text":"Social-media trends"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Cultural movements"},{"text":"Colour trends"},{"text":"Fabric trends"},{"text":"Silhouette trends"},{"text":"Youth culture"},{"text":"Celebrity influence"},{"text":"Retail trends"},{"text":"Emerging designers"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a monthly trend report during college."},{"type":"p","text":"A good stylist should be able to distinguish between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Temporary viral trend","emerging trend","commercial trend","long-term fashion direction"]}]},{"heading":"Mood boards and concept development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build professional mood boards containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept statement"},{"text":"Colour palette"},{"text":"Garments"},{"text":"Fabrics"},{"text":"Accessories"},{"text":"Hair direction"},{"text":"Makeup direction"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Photography references"},{"text":"Typography"},{"text":"Pose references"},{"text":"Brand references"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Illustrator"},{"text":"InDesign"},{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Pinterest-style research boards"},{"text":"Presentation software"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The mood board should communicate a clear creative direction, not simply collect attractive images."}]},{"heading":"Photography and shoot production","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A stylist should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lighting basics"},{"text":"Camera angles"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Posing"},{"text":"Location"},{"text":"Background"},{"text":"Colour grading"},{"text":"Image references"},{"text":"Shot lists"},{"text":"Editorial sequencing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how clothing appears differently in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Studio photography"},{"text":"Outdoor photography"},{"text":"Runway"},{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"Video"},{"text":"Social media"},{"text":"Editorial photography"}]}]},{"heading":"Hair, makeup and grooming coordination","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A stylist does not necessarily need to become a professional makeup artist or hairstylist."},{"type":"p","text":"However, understand enough to coordinate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hair direction"},{"text":"Makeup mood"},{"text":"Grooming"},{"text":"Accessories"},{"text":"Nails"},{"text":"Overall styling consistency"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Minimal clothing","clean hair","natural makeup","architectural jewellery"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"creates a very different visual message from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Maximalist clothing","dramatic makeup","statement accessories."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Fashion software and digital tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build working proficiency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adobe Photoshop"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Adobe InDesign"},{"text":"Lightroom or equivalent"},{"text":"Canva for rapid presentations"},{"text":"Figma for digital boards/presentations"},{"text":"Spreadsheet tools for wardrobe inventories and budgets"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is not software certification. The objective is being able to communicate and execute a styling concept professionally."}]},{"heading":"Fashion business skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional stylist needs more than creative taste."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Budgeting"},{"text":"Vendor coordination"},{"text":"Garment sourcing"},{"text":"Rental management"},{"text":"Purchase tracking"},{"text":"Returns"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Invoicing"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Client communication"},{"text":"Scheduling"},{"text":"Production planning"},{"text":"Team coordination"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to create a simple:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Styling brief","Budget","Sourcing list","Shoot schedule","Outfit list","Call sheet","Shoot","Returns","Final delivery"]}]},{"heading":"Brand understanding","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Luxury brands"},{"text":"Premium fashion"},{"text":"Fast fashion"},{"text":"D2C brands"},{"text":"Streetwear"},{"text":"Sportswear"},{"text":"Sustainable fashion"},{"text":"Indian ethnic wear"},{"text":"Contemporary Indian fashion"},{"text":"Couture"},{"text":"Bridal fashion"},{"text":"Accessories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how styling changes according to brand identity and target customer."},{"type":"h","text":"AI for fashion styling"},{"type":"p","text":"AI can support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trend research"},{"text":"Mood-board exploration"},{"text":"Colour exploration"},{"text":"Styling concept generation"},{"text":"Image reference generation"},{"text":"Outfit variations"},{"text":"Product categorisation"},{"text":"Fashion copy"},{"text":"Shoot planning"},{"text":"Background exploration"},{"text":"Content repurposing"},{"text":"Virtual styling concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, human judgement remains critical for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fit"},{"text":"Fabric"},{"text":"Cultural context"},{"text":"Brand identity"},{"text":"Authenticity"},{"text":"Client preferences"},{"text":"Garment quality"},{"text":"Ethical sourcing"},{"text":"Final styling decisions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Future stylists should learn to work through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Brief","Research","AI-assisted exploration","Human selection","Garment sourcing","Physical styling","Photography/video","Final campaign"]},{"type":"h","text":"Styling portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"A weak portfolio:"},{"type":"p","text":"A collection of fashion illustrations and college garments."},{"type":"p","text":"A stronger Stylist portfolio:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Brief","Concept","Mood Board","Fashion Research","Garment Selection","Accessories","Hair/Makeup Direction","Shoot","Final Images","Styling Rationale"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build 6–10 strong styling stories."},{"type":"p","text":"Recommended projects:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Editorial fashion story"},{"text":"Personal styling project"},{"text":"Celebrity-inspired editorial concept"},{"text":"E-commerce styling project"},{"text":"Indian contemporary fashion shoot"},{"text":"Sustainable fashion styling"},{"text":"Streetwear campaign"},{"text":"Luxury-fashion campaign"},{"text":"Bridal/occasion styling"},{"text":"Fashion-film styling"},{"text":"Seasonal trend campaign"},{"text":"AI-assisted fashion concept with human styling execution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Styling specialisation options"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Editorial Styling"},{"text":"Fashion + photography + storytelling"},{"text":"Senior Fashion Stylist"}],[{"text":"Celebrity Styling"},{"text":"Personal styling + luxury + events"},{"text":"Celebrity Stylist"}],[{"text":"Personal Styling"},{"text":"Wardrobe + client psychology + shopping"},{"text":"Personal Stylist / Image Consultant"}],[{"text":"Commercial Styling"},{"text":"Brand + campaign + retail"},{"text":"Commercial Stylist"}],[{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"Product styling + photography + speed"},{"text":"E-commerce Styling Lead"}],[{"text":"Fashion Campaigns"},{"text":"Art direction + branding + production"},{"text":"Fashion Art Director"}],[{"text":"Runway"},{"text":"Collection + show production + styling"},{"text":"Fashion Show Stylist"}],[{"text":"Film/TV"},{"text":"Character + wardrobe + continuity"},{"text":"Costume/Styling Specialist"}],[{"text":"Bridal"},{"text":"Occasionwear + client management"},{"text":"Bridal Stylist"}],[{"text":"Men's Styling"},{"text":"Menswear + grooming + tailoring"},{"text":"Menswear Stylist"}],[{"text":"Sustainable Fashion"},{"text":"Circular fashion + sourcing"},{"text":"Sustainable Fashion Consultant"}],[{"text":"Digital/Social"},{"text":"Content + trends + short-form video"},{"text":"Fashion Content Creative Lead"}],[{"text":"Accessories"},{"text":"Jewellery + bags + footwear"},{"text":"Accessories Stylist"}],[{"text":"Fashion Direction"},{"text":"Styling + brand + leadership"},{"text":"Fashion/Creative Director"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant, 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"The styling profession will increasingly combine physical fashion expertise with digital content, AI, virtual fashion, e-commerce and creative direction."},{"type":"p","text":"Future capabilities should include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted styling"},{"text":"Virtual try-on"},{"text":"3D fashion"},{"text":"Digital garments"},{"text":"AR fashion experiences"},{"text":"Virtual showrooms"},{"text":"Fashion e-commerce optimisation"},{"text":"Personalised styling"},{"text":"Sustainable wardrobe systems"},{"text":"Circular fashion"},{"text":"Data-driven trend forecasting"},{"text":"Social-commerce content"},{"text":"Fashion-film production"},{"text":"Creative direction"}]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government, cultural and public-sector opportunities"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation/category","What to seek"],"rows":[[{"text":"Ministry of Textiles ecosystem"},{"text":"Textile/fashion exposure"}],[{"text":"Textiles Committee"},{"text":"Textile and industry exposure"}],[{"text":"National Institute of Fashion Technology ecosystem"},{"text":"Fashion/design projects where available"}],[{"text":"Handloom/handicrafts organisations"},{"text":"Indian textile and craft styling"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Culture institutions"},{"text":"Costume, heritage and exhibition-related projects"}],[{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Costume/fashion collections and documentation"}],[{"text":"State Handloom/Handicrafts departments"},{"text":"Regional textiles and crafts"}],[{"text":"Government design/skill programmes"},{"text":"Fashion communication and design exposure"}],[{"text":"PM Internship Scheme"},{"text":"Structured industry exposure, subject to current eligibility"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A useful starting point for textile-sector information is Ministry of Textiles.","url":"https://texmin.nic.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Private / industry"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fashion houses"},{"text":"Designer labels"},{"text":"Apparel brands"},{"text":"Luxury brands"},{"text":"E-commerce fashion companies"},{"text":"Fashion magazines"},{"text":"Editorial publications"},{"text":"Fashion photographers"},{"text":"Celebrity stylists"},{"text":"Personal styling companies"},{"text":"Image-consulting firms"},{"text":"Advertising agencies"},{"text":"Creative agencies"},{"text":"Production houses"},{"text":"Fashion PR agencies"},{"text":"Fashion influencers/content creators"},{"text":"Fashion-event companies"},{"text":"Bridal studios"},{"text":"Costume departments"},{"text":"Fashion marketplaces"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For early experience, assisting a working stylist on real shoots can be especially valuable, because it exposes the student to sourcing, fittings, last-minute changes, vendors, models and production schedules."}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification / learning area","Why it helps"],"rows":[[{"text":"Fashion styling"},{"text":"Core professional skill"}],[{"text":"Fashion merchandising"},{"text":"Commercial understanding"}],[{"text":"Fashion forecasting"},{"text":"Trend research"}],[{"text":"Personal styling"},{"text":"Client-facing styling"}],[{"text":"Image consulting"},{"text":"Personal/client styling"}],[{"text":"Fashion photography"},{"text":"Shoot collaboration"}],[{"text":"Adobe Photoshop"},{"text":"Image editing"}],[{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Fashion/design communication"}],[{"text":"InDesign"},{"text":"Editorial work"}],[{"text":"Fashion communication"},{"text":"Visual storytelling"}],[{"text":"Social-media content"},{"text":"Digital fashion marketing"}],[{"text":"Sustainable fashion"},{"text":"Future-facing fashion practice"}],[{"text":"Visual merchandising"},{"text":"Retail styling"}],[{"text":"Fashion business"},{"text":"Commercial awareness"}],[{"text":"AI for creative industries"},{"text":"Emerging workflow"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Certificates should support the portfolio rather than replace it."}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Realistic first-job titles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Styling Intern"},{"text":"Styling Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Assistant"},{"text":"Wardrobe Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Coordinator"},{"text":"Junior Stylist"},{"text":"Assistant Fashion Stylist"},{"text":"E-commerce Styling Assistant"},{"text":"Editorial Styling Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Production Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Content Assistant"},{"text":"Visual Merchandising Assistant"},{"text":"Personal Styling Assistant"},{"text":"Costume Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Editorial Assistant"},{"text":"Fashion Design Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Progression roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stylist"},{"text":"Fashion Stylist"},{"text":"Senior Stylist"},{"text":"Celebrity Stylist"},{"text":"Lead Stylist"},{"text":"Commercial Stylist"},{"text":"Fashion Editor"},{"text":"Fashion Art Director"},{"text":"Creative Director"},{"text":"Fashion Director"}]},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Stack the posting asks for","Where the student proves it"],"rows":[[{"text":"Styling Assistant"},{"text":"Garments + sourcing + organisation"},{"text":"Shoot experience"}],[{"text":"Junior Stylist"},{"text":"Styling + trends + visual sense"},{"text":"Styling portfolio"}],[{"text":"Fashion Stylist"},{"text":"Styling + client/brand understanding"},{"text":"Published/commercial work"}],[{"text":"Personal Stylist"},{"text":"Wardrobe + client communication"},{"text":"Client styling cases"}],[{"text":"E-commerce Stylist"},{"text":"Product styling + speed + consistency"},{"text":"E-commerce case study"}],[{"text":"Editorial Stylist"},{"text":"Concept + fashion + photography"},{"text":"Editorial portfolio"}],[{"text":"Celebrity Stylist"},{"text":"Luxury + sourcing + client management"},{"text":"Event/editorial experience"}],[{"text":"Fashion Art Director"},{"text":"Styling + brand + creative leadership"},{"text":"Integrated campaign portfolio"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career reality"},{"type":"p","text":"Stylist is accessible as an entry-level pathway, but established stylist careers are strongly portfolio-, reputation- and network-driven."},{"type":"p","text":"The student's first role may be Styling Assistant or Fashion Assistant, rather than simply “Stylist.”"}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate degree is not mandatory for becoming a Stylist. Industry experience, portfolio, contacts and demonstrated styling ability are often more important."},{"type":"table","header":["PG option","Useful for"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Des Fashion Design"},{"text":"Advanced fashion/design practice"}],[{"text":"M.Des Fashion Communication"},{"text":"Styling + visual communication"}],[{"text":"M.Des Fashion Management"},{"text":"Fashion business"}],[{"text":"M.Des Accessory Design"},{"text":"Accessories specialisation"}],[{"text":"MA Fashion Communication"},{"text":"Editorial/communication"}],[{"text":"MA Fashion Design"},{"text":"Advanced design"}],[{"text":"Fashion Management"},{"text":"Brand and commercial roles"}],[{"text":"Fashion Merchandising"},{"text":"Retail/commercial fashion"}],[{"text":"Fashion Marketing"},{"text":"Brand strategy"}],[{"text":"Luxury Brand Management"},{"text":"Luxury fashion"}],[{"text":"Visual Communication"},{"text":"Editorial/creative direction"}],[{"text":"MBA Marketing"},{"text":"Commercial fashion leadership"}],[{"text":"MBA Luxury Brand Management"},{"text":"Luxury-sector management"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD routes"},{"type":"p","text":"For research and academic careers:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fashion Design"},{"text":"Fashion Studies"},{"text":"Fashion Communication"},{"text":"Fashion Management"},{"text":"Textile Studies"},{"text":"Design Studies"},{"text":"Visual Culture"},{"text":"Costume Studies"},{"text":"Cultural Studies"},{"text":"Sustainable Fashion"},{"text":"Design Research"}]}]},{"heading":"Study abroad, country by country","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Example universities/institutions to investigate","Scholarship route","Gate to check"],"rows":[[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Central Saint Martins/UAL, London College of Fashion/UAL, RCA, Kingston"},{"text":"University funding, Chevening where applicable"},{"text":"Portfolio + programme requirements"}],[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Parsons, FIT, SCAD, Pratt"},{"text":"University scholarships, Fulbright"},{"text":"Portfolio + English + finances"}],[{"text":"Italy"},{"text":"Polimoda, Istituto Marangoni, NABA and relevant universities"},{"text":"Institution/regional funding"},{"text":"Portfolio + programme fit"}],[{"text":"France"},{"text":"Fashion/design schools and universities"},{"text":"Institution/government opportunities"},{"text":"Language + portfolio"}],[{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Public design/fashion programmes"},{"text":"DAAD"},{"text":"Programme language + portfolio"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Fashion/design institutions"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Portfolio + eligibility"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"RMIT and relevant design schools"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Portfolio + English"}],[{"text":"Japan"},{"text":"Fashion/design universities"},{"text":"MEXT"},{"text":"Language + programme requirements"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fashion/styling portfolio"},{"text":"Mood boards"},{"text":"Editorial shoots"},{"text":"Styling case studies"},{"text":"Design projects"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"Statement of purpose"},{"text":"Academic transcripts"},{"text":"Recommendation letters"},{"text":"English-language test where required"},{"text":"Financial documents"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For scholarship exploration, use official sources such as DAAD India and USIEF.","url":"https://www.daad.in/en/"},{"type":"note","label":"Verify","text":"current university portfolios, tuition, scholarships, deadlines, language requirements and visa/post-study rules."}]},{"heading":"Going forward","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Fashion Design Student","Styling Intern","Styling/Fashion Assistant","Junior Stylist","Stylist","Senior / Lead Stylist","Fashion Art Director / Fashion Editor","Creative Director / Fashion Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative long-term paths"},{"type":"p","text":"A Stylist can eventually move into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Celebrity Styling"},{"text":"Editorial Styling"},{"text":"Personal Styling"},{"text":"Image Consulting"},{"text":"Fashion Art Direction"},{"text":"Fashion Photography Direction"},{"text":"Fashion Editorial"},{"text":"Fashion Marketing"},{"text":"Fashion Buying"},{"text":"Fashion Merchandising"},{"text":"Fashion Content Creation"},{"text":"Fashion Brand Strategy"},{"text":"Luxury Brand Management"},{"text":"Costume Design"},{"text":"Fashion Entrepreneurship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future Stylist will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Fashion Knowledge","Styling","Trend Intelligence","Photography","Brand Strategy","Digital Content","AI","Sustainability","Business Skills"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"AI may automate parts of visual ideation and product matching, but physical garment knowledge, fit, taste, cultural understanding, human relationships, sourcing and creative judgement remain valuable differentiators."}]}]}